==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[don't cry over spilled milk]]

===Proverb===
{{infl|en|proverb|head=[[don't]] [[cry]] [[over]] [[spilt]] [[milk]]}}

# It is no use [[worry]]ing about [[unfortunate]] [[event]]s which have [[already]] [[happen]]ed and which cannot be [[change]]d.

====Translations====
{{trans-top|it is no use worrying about unfortunate events which have already happened}}
* Arabic: {{t|ar|لا تبك على الحليب المسكوب}}
* Chinese: [[覆水難收]], [[覆水难收]] (fù shuǐ nán shōu)
* Czech: {{t-|cs|neplač nad rozlitým mlékem}}
* Finnish: [[ei kannata itkeä kaatunutta maitoa]]
* Hebrew: {{t|he|אין בוכים על חלב שנשפך}}
* Icelandic: {{t|is|ekki er hægt að sjá við öllum leka}}
* Irish: {{t|ga|Níl maith sa seanchas nuair a bhíos an anachain déanta|xs=Irish}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Italian: [[non piangere sul latte versato]]; [[inutile piangere sul latte versato]]
* Japanese: [[覆水盆に返らず]] (ふくすいぼんにかえらず, fukusui bon ni kaerazu)
* Norwegian: {{t|no|ikke gråt over spilt melk}}
* Polish: {{t|pl|nie płacz nad rozlanym mlekiem}}
* Portuguese: [[não chore sobre o leite derramado]]
* Russian: {{t-|ru|о пролитом молоке не плачут|tr=o prolítom moloké ne pláčut}}
* Spanish: [[no llorar sobre la leche derramada]], [[no llorar por la leche derramada]]
* Swedish: [[gråt inte över spilld mjölk]]
{{trans-bottom}}

{{checktrans-top}}
* {{ttbc|French}}: Il ne faut pas pleurer sur le lait renversé. The origin may be found in a fable by [[w:Jean de La Fontaine|Jean de La Fontaine]], ''la laitière et le pot au lait'' (the milkmaid and the milkpot) ; but the poet borrowed themes from [[w:Aesop|Aesop]].
{{trans-bottom}}

